# Content surfaces. See ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md for what they mean, and
# docs/specs/2026-08-02-content-surfaces.md for why.
#
#   human-only      the user owns it; the agent never edits it
#   human-revised   the agent edits it; reviewed=<sha> is what the user read through
#   unlisted        the agent edits it, no review tracking
#
# Patterns must be path-anchored, and a trailing slash matches nothing here —
# use `dir/**`. Leave this file unlisted, or the agent cannot write the stamp.
#
# No human-only path is declared yet. The syntax, when you want one:
#   docs/some-file.md             surface=human-only

plugins/*/skills/*/SKILL.md       surface=human-revised reviewed=c420771
plugins/*/skills/*/references/**  surface=human-revised reviewed=c420771
